                            Residual mis-attribution risk (mid-function CC runs) is disclosed;
                            per-site windows + extents are printed so anomalies show.
  ESCAPE-CHANNEL RULE   = a token present in EAX/ECX/EDX at a call, or in a stack slot at an
                            argument position (address >= current esp), is an ESCAPE; it is
                            classified by the callee head. clobbered_before_use (the channel's
                            value destroyed inside the walked head without use) marks the escape
                            NON-EFFECTIVE; the site's other channels then decide.
  DISPOSITION PRIORITY (pre-registered, deterministic):
    1 direct WRITE_S events (offsets 0/4/8 = triple writes; others = other-offset writes)
    2 effective escape with head WRITE_THROUGH        -> S_PTR_ESCAPED_WRITE
    3 effective escape with head FORWARDED / NOT_USED_IN_CHECKED_HEAD -> S_PTR_ESCAPED_UNRESOLVED
    4 effective escape with head INSUFFICIENT_PROOF_HEAD_BOUND -> INSUFFICIENT_PROOF_HEAD_BOUND
    5 all effective escapes READ_ONLY                  -> S_PTR_ESCAPED_READ_ONLY
    6 ESCAPE_STORE (stored into another object/global)  -> S_PTR_ESCAPED_UNRESOLVED
    7 ESCAPE_AT_TERMINAL with live register tokens      -> S_PTR_ESCAPED_UNRESOLVED (returned to
      the enclosing caller; that caller is outside this site's window and unanalyzed here)
    8 stack-model ambiguity (AMBIG_EBP/SPILL_UNKNOWN_EBP/AMBIG_STACK/ESP_PIVOT, or
      ESP_UNCERTAIN with live/possible spill state) with live/possible spill -> INSUFFICIENT_PROOF_STACK_ESCAPE
    9 unconditional jmp with live tokens -> CONTROL_FLOW_ESCAPE
   10 conditional branch crossed while provenance live (taken path unexamined) -> CONTROL_FLOW_ESCAPE
   11 window exhausted with spill-live tokens only -> INSUFFICIENT_PROOF_STACK_ESCAPE;
      with register-live tokens -> INSUFFICIENT_PROOF; with all tokens dead:
      destruction events present -> S_PROVENANCE_LOST else NO_WRITE_WITHIN_BOUND
